            "description": "Co-managed LASIK is a vision-correcting procedure where an eye care provider collaborates with a LASIK surgeon: providing pre-operative evaluation, surgical guidance, and post-operative management. LASIK complications may include infection (approx. 1 in 1,500 cases), glare or halos, under- or over-correction, dry eye, temporary visual fluctuations.",
